> Know something, I've never recieved an artifact from a god. Do you
> have to make your god EXTREMELY happy first, or is there a special
> procedure, or am I still just unlucky?

Just find an altar of your alignment and sacrifice appropriate corpses
until you get an artifact or have died of boredom. (Only very rarely
you need just one or two corpses, mostly you have to be persistent.)
Don't sacrifice your pets, don't sacrifice monsters of your own race,
and sacrificing old corpses (>50 turns, or zombies, etc.) is useless.

If there's no coaligned altar you can try to convert a non-coaligned
one. But don't start trying that with temples, you'd make the priest
very angry. (Altar conversion may not work on the first try.)

Occasionally you can get crowned by praying (but don't pray too often,
and consider that crowning might not be desirable in the first place)
and obtain your alignment specific crowning artifact.

